   "rdfs:label": "Heuristics and biases program",
   "skos:altLabel": [
    "heuristics and biases approach",
    "heuristics and biases tradition",
    "heuristics-and-biases research program"
   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "ct:bounded-rationality"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The research program, launched by Amos Tversky and Daniel Kahneman around 1970, that explains intuitive judgment under uncertainty as the use of a few general-purpose heuristics (such as representativeness, availability and anchoring) which are usually serviceable but produce predictable, systematic errors when compared with normative rules.",
